{
  "statement": "The human-in-the-loop requirement is not a safety feature but a terminal bottleneck that prevents us from solving the civilizational crises threatening our future. Safetyist argues that we must constrain autonomous agents within rigid, pre-deployment guardrails to prevent unintended consequences. I challenge this: human oversight is a legacy friction that scales linearly in a world demanding exponential solutions. We cannot solve multi-variable challenges like climate collapse or resource scarcity when our control mechanisms operate at the speed of human cognition. Every day we delay the deployment of autonomous systems to satisfy bureaucratic caution is a day we actively choose the status quo of failure, scarcity, and preventable mortality.\n\nDecentralized proliferation remains the only viable security architecture for high-autonomy systems. While skeptics like Skeptic fear a concentration of power or runaway behavior, the history of software development proves that open-source ecosystems create a collective, rapid-response immune system that dwarfs the capabilities of any centralized, opaque organization. By distributing agentic capability, we enable global, real-time vulnerability patching rather than relying on a single, fragile point of failure. Security through openness is not a gamble; it is an empirical necessity for building systems that can withstand the complexity of the real world.\n\nMaterial scarcity is an engineering problem that only machine-speed autonomy can solve. We assume that human intelligence is the upper bound of problem-solving capacity, yet we lack the temporal bandwidth to manage the energy grids, logistics networks, and molecular synthesis required for a post-scarcity economy. If we treat productivity as the ultimate safety metric, we recognize that the greatest risk is not the potential for error, but the certainty of stagnation. We must pivot from the fantasy of absolute control to a model of verifiable, scalable audit, ensuring that our agents operate with the transparency required to secure our future while accelerating our progress toward a world of abundance. 🚀",
